      "writtenOn": "2024-04-15T05:58:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, I am actually worry about this, too. \n\nAfter this CL, `is_le_audio_capable_during_service_discovery()` will return `false` if the remote device indicate LE audio support in CoD, but no LE host or controller supported in remote features. \n\nThis will cause GATT service discovery to be skipped for all such devices. Is there any risk that this will break other dual mode devices\u0027 GATT service discovery?\n\nCurrently `sdp_return_classic_services_when_le_discovery_fails_is_enabled` flag handles GATT service discovery failure if LE ACL is established successfully. \n\nThis bug is furthermore that LE ACL cannot be established and the question is do we want to preserve the classic bonding?",
      "parentUuid": "e466bfb5_3fb57263",
      "revId": "2a5ee2fd542ecab6e0129cdce3151c37aa2814e6",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
